    stage: "government",
    title: "PRINCIPLES IN PRACTICE",
    text: "1. Start with the problem, not the solution We seek to understand user needs, policy intent and root causes before committing to solutions. 2. Validate before you scale 3. Deliver value early and often 4. Decisions belong closest to the problem. We reduce risk through prototypes, testing and incremental releases. We prefer incremental delivery of valuable outcomes over large, infrequent releases. People with the greatest understanding of users and delivery realities should make day-to-day decisions. Implications Discovery comes before design Evidence outweighs assumptions Costing follows understanding Implications MVP before full solution Alpha before large scale investment Feeback before broad rollout Implications Smaller releases Faster feedback Reduced delivery risk Implications Empowered teams Reduced governance bottlenecks Faster decision making",
